[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:10. The Loss of the Titanic]
[00:00.960] Passage 10. | 第10篇课文。
[00:02.010] The loss of the Titanic. | 泰坦尼克号的沉没。
[00:04.790] The great ship Titanic sailed for New York from Southampton on April the 10th, 1912. | 1912年4月10日，巨轮泰坦尼克号从南安普敦启程驶往纽约。
[00:11.980] She was carrying 1,316 passengers and a crew of 891. | 船上载有1,316名乘客和891名船员。
[00:18.400] Even by modern standards, the 66,000-ton Titanic was a colossal ship. | 即使按现代标准衡量，66,000吨的泰坦尼克号也是一艘巨轮。
[00:24.690] At that time, however, she was not only the largest ship that had ever been built, | 然而，在那个时代，它不仅是当时建造的最大的船只，
[00:29.710] but was regarded as unsinkable, | 而且被认为是永不沉没的，
[00:32.070] for she had 16 watertight compartments. | 因为它有16个水密舱。
[00:35.465] Even if two of these were flooded, she would still be able to float. | 即使其中两个舱进水，它也能漂浮在水面上。
[00:39.840] The tragic sinking of this great liner will always be remembered, | 这艘巨轮的悲惨沉没将永远被人们铭记，
[00:44.005] for she went down on her first voyage with heavy loss of life. | 因为它在首航中沉没，造成了重大的生命损失。
[00:48.665] Four days after setting out, | 启航4天后，
[00:51.640] while the Titanic was sailing across the icy waters of the North Atlantic, | 当泰坦尼克号航行在北大西洋冰冷的海水中时，
[00:55.675] a huge iceberg was suddenly spotted by a lookout. | 一名瞭望员突然发现了一座巨大的冰山。
[00:59.740] After the alarm had been given, | 警报发出后，
[01:02.080] the great ship turned sharply to avoid a direct collision. | 这艘巨轮急转弯，以避免直接碰撞。
[01:06.130] The Titanic turned just in time, | 泰坦尼克号及时转向，
[01:08.730] narrowly missing the immense wall of ice which rose over 100 feet out of the water beside her. | 险些擦过船旁边高出水面100多英尺的巨大冰墙。
[01:15.005] Suddenly, | 突然，
[01:16.390] there was a slight trembling sound from below, | 船舱下方传来轻微的颤抖声，
[01:19.385] and the captain went down to see what had happened. | 船长下去查看发生了什么。
[01:22.315] The noise had been so faint that no one thought that the ship had been damaged. | 声音如此微弱，没有人认为船只受损了。
[01:27.510] Below, the captain realized to his horror, | 在下面，船长惊恐地意识到，
[01:30.870] that the Titanic was sinking rapidly. | 泰坦尼克号正在迅速下沉。
[01:33.295] For five of her 16 watertight compartments had already been flooded. | 因为它的16个水密舱中已有5个进水。
[01:38.600] The order to abandon ship was given, | 弃船的命令下达了，
[01:41.450] and hundreds of people plunged into the icy water. | 数百人跳入了冰冷的海水中。
[01:44.975] As there were not enough lifeboats for everybody, | 由于没有足够的救生艇供所有人使用，
[01:48.205] 1,500 lives were lost. | 1,500条生命逝去了。